Z||000001||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||10:06 AM||||wannabe,<P>What exactly do you want pictued?  I have one in pieces all over my garage floor.  The intent is to install it in the next few weeks.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||10-26-2000||10:20 AM||||I wouldn't mind seeing pics as well, I'd like to eventually swap the whole rear suspension setup from an 88 into an 86 GT.<P>as for the front I'll probably just use drop springs etc.. and hopefully konis all around.. heh. (all depends on $$$$$)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick's Dad||10-26-2000||10:55 AM||||Those who know better, correct me if I'm wrong....<P>If I recall correctly, the mounting points for the 88 suspension are different than the 84-87's. The trailing arm pivot point would need to be drilled, and these may not be the only differences that (may have?) precipitated a different engine cradle.<P>I suppose that I could check the part numbers, but my son seems to be failing to change his clothes without my direct supervision....<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||10-26-2000||11:09 AM||||I'd like to get a look at the general configuration, how many radius rods, where the trailing links mount and how the links attach to the spindle. A picture of the spindle itself would actually be very helpful.||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||11:53 AM||||Friends,<P>Sorry for the length... those of you that know me, understand that brevity and tact are not some of my strengths.  I will try my best to take digital pics (THANKS FIERO56) of not only each component, but also the assembly and swap.  Please be patient.  I have a timeline of a few months before I expect to have this thing back in entirely.  The component pics should be done in a few days.  <P>DaRkLoRD,<P>I will post them to the forum with pip so everyone can get the information.  My 88 rear suspension is going into my 86 SE project vehicle.  Your idea sounds cool and similar to mine, but I am using a Ryane coil-over kit in the rear and Street Dreams drop spindles in the front.  I will need to up the front springs with aftermarket though because of the stiffness that I chose for the rear. <P>Patrick's Dad,<P>You are correct!  An 88 engine cradle, connecting rods, spindles, etc are all needed.  I would not try to modify an 84-87 cradle to accept the new geometry.  Not only would it be FUGLY, but it would require much more work than I want to exert.  <P>Wannabe,<P>I will try to show the number and general configuration of radius rods & assoc. connection points before I transfer the engine to the 88 cradle.  That way you should get a good view of what it entails.  The spindles will be easy to snap a picture of.  <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||10-26-2000||01:03 PM||||Hmm.. I was under the impression that the 88 rear suspension was a direct bolt-in but the front wouldn't work on 84-87 cars..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||01:44 PM||||darklord,<P>You are correct... I must have not been clear in my post.  The 88 front set-up cannot be easily converted as the main frame section is of a different geometry.  The rear in my 86 is getting the 88 suspension and Ryane coil-over kit.  The front is just getting the Street Dreams spindles and new stiffer springs... maybe a different swaybar eventually.  <P>Sorry for the confusion,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
